{"agent":"fleet-reviewtree","data":{"by":"deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash","evidence":{"chunk_findings":[{"chunk":2,"detail":"`_misplaced` only reaches the new `wrong_tree_refusal(...)` call when `closed_item_refusal(...)` returned an *empty* `why` **and** an empty `_note`:\n\n```python\nwhy, _note = ( ... closed_item_refusal(it, force=force, reason=reason, ...) )\nif not why and _note == \"\" and not (branch or commit):\n    why = wrong_tree_refusal(repo, _load(repo, agent)[2], it, called_from)\n```\n\n`closed_item_refusal` is the helper that waives the \"do not record on a COMPLETE item\" rule when `--force` is given; in the waived case it does not refuse (`why == \"\"`) but returns a non-empty note recording the override. So the `_note == \"\"` term is false exactly on the documented override path, and the wrong-tree check is skipped. Concrete input: item `B` is COMPLETE; the caller's cwd is item `A`'s worktree; run `ddflow review B --gate rubber_duck --force`. `closed_item_refusal` yields `(\"\", <force note>)`, `not why and _note == \"\"` is false, `wrong_tree_refusal` is never consulted, the review diffs item `A`'s tree, and a `rubber_duck` gate is recorded against `B` from the wrong diff — i.e. exactly the stray-gate scenario of B8b2dafcbf3, merely behind `--force`. The `--force` flag is scoped by the intent to the COMPLETE-item refusal (\"refuses to record on a COMPLETE item without `--force`\"); it should not also disable the wrong-tree guard, which is the primary fix here. Any state in which `closed_item_refusal` returns note-without-refusal makes the wrong-tree branch dead for that call, so the new guard is not unconditional.","digest":"bb8137989717d8a7","location":"ddflow/api/review.py:_misplaced (the `_note == \"\"` guard, ~line 1278)","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"ddflow/api/review.py:_misplaced (the `_note == \"\"` guard, ~line 1278)"}],"chunks_total":3,"coverage":"3/3 chunk(s) reviewed","delta_rounds":0,"diff_chars":10998,"diff_sha":"549b11688823888f5